// TEST: MUST_FAIL — a bare (non-`~`) top-level module-qualified Koru statement in
//       a `.kz` file is rejected LOUDLY at the parser, located at the user's source.
//
// In `.kz`, top-level Koru flow statements require the `~` prefix (a `.k` file
// auto-synthesizes it). Before the fix, a bare `std/io:print.ln(...)` was SWALLOWED
// — pasted verbatim into output_emitted.zig, dying with a cryptic Zig error
// (`expected ',' after field`) instead of a clean frontend diagnostic. The parser
// now recognizes the `<path>/<seg>:<name>` shape as a bare Koru construct (PARSE003).
~import std/io

std/io:print.ln("hi")
